hadiths[22]{hadithnumber,text}:
"18112","Yahya ibn Saeed narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj who said: Ata informed me that Safwan ibn Yala ibn Umayyah informed him that Yala used to say to Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah the Exalted be pleased with him: Would that I could see the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when revelation is sent down to him. He said: When he was at al-Jiranah, with a garment over the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, shading him, and with him were people from his Companions, among them Umar, a man came to him wearing a jubbah, saturated with perfume. He said: So he said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you think of a man who entered ihram for umrah wearing a jubbah after saturating himself with perfume? The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, looked for a while, then fell silent, then revelation came to him. So Umar signaled to Yala to come, so Yala came and put his head in, and behold the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with red face, thus for a while, then it was relieved from him. So he said: Where is the one who asked me about umrah just now? The man was sought and brought to him. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: As for the perfume that is on you, wash it three times, and as for the jubbah, take it off, then do in your umrah as you do in your pilgrimage."
"18113","Yahya ibn Saeed narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj who said: Ata informed me, Safwan ibn Yala ibn Umayyah informed me, from his father who said: My hired worker fought a man and bit his hand, so he pulled his hand from his mouth, knocking out his front tooth. So he came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who voided it and said: Does he leave his hand in your mouth for you to chomp it as the stallion chomps?"
"18114","Bahz ibn Asad narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Ata, from Safwan ibn Yala ibn Umayyah, from his father, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: When my messengers come to you, give them thirty coats of mail and thirty camels, or less than that. So he said to him: Is the loan guaranteed, O Messenger of Allah? He said: So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Yes."
"18115","Abdur-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Atiq informed me, from Abdullah ibn Babayah, from some of the sons of Yala ibn Umayyah, from Yala ibn Umayyah who said: I was with Umar, may Allah the Exalted be pleased with him, and he touched the Corner. Yala said: And I was on the side next to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. When I reached the western Corner which is next to the Black one, I slipped forward before him to touch it. So he said: What is the matter with you? I said: Will you not touch these two? He said: Did you not circumambulate with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him? I said: Yes indeed. He said: Did you see him touch these two, meaning the two western ones? I said: No. He said: Then you have no good example in that. I said: Yes indeed. He said: Then pass on past you."
"18116","Abdullah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from a man, from Ibn Yala, from Yala who said: I saw the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with his upper garment wrapped under his right arm and over his left shoulder, wearing a Hadrami cloak."
"18117","Yaqoub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq who said: Ata ibn Abi Rabah narrated to me, from Safwan ibn Abdullah ibn Safwan, from his two uncles Yala ibn Umayyah and Salamah ibn Umayyah who said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in the expedition of Tabuk, with a companion of ours with us. He and a man from the Muslims fought each other, so that man bit his forearm, so he pulled his hand from his mouth, knocking out his front tooth. So the man went to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, asking for blood-money. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: One of you goes to his brother and bites him as the stallion bites, then he comes seeking blood-money? You have no blood-money. He said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, voided it, meaning he annulled it."
"18118","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Ibn Yala, from Yala, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, like the hadith of Qatadah from Zurarah from Imran, concerning the one who is bitten by one of them."
"18119","Umar ibn Harun al-Balkhi, Abu Hafs, narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from some of the sons of Yala ibn Umayyah, from his father who said: I saw the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with his garment wrapped under his right arm between al-Safa and al-Marwah, wearing a Najrani cloak."
"18120","Waki narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ibn Yala, from his father, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he arrived, circumambulated the House while wrapping a Hadrami cloak of his under his right arm."
"18121","Al-Haytham ibn Kharijah narrated to us, he said: Bashir ibn Talhah, Abu Nasr al-Hadrami or al-Khushani, narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Durayk, from Yala ibn Umayyah who said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to send me on detachments, and one day he sent me on a detachment. A man was riding a mule, so I said to him: Mount, for the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, has sent me on a detachment. He said: I will not go out with you. I said: Why? He said: Until you guarantee me three dinars. I said: Now that I have bidden farewell to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, I will not return to him; mount, and you shall have three dinars. When I returned from my expedition, I mentioned that to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: He has nothing from this expedition of his, neither of his worldly nor of his hereafter, except the three dinars."
"18122","Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Layth, meaning Ibn Saad, narrated to us, he said: Uqayl ibn Khalid narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, from Amr ibn Abdur-Rahman ibn Umayyah, that his father informed him that Yala said: I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with my father Umayyah on the day of the Conquest, and said: O Messenger of Allah, pledge my father for emigration. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Rather I will pledge him for jihad, for emigration has ended."
"18123","Abu Asim narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Umayyah ibn Abi Uthman al-Qurashi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Huyayy ibn Yala ibn Umayyah narrated to us, from his father who said: I saw Yala pray before the sun rose, so a man said to him, or it was said to him: You are a man from the Companions of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, yet you pray before the sun rises? Yala said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: The sun rises between the two horns of Satan. Yala said to him: For the sun to rise while you are engaged in the affair of Allah is better than for it to rise while you are heedless."
"18124","Abu Asim narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Umayyah narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Huyayy narrated to me, he said: Safwan ibn Yala narrated to me, from his father, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The sea is Hell. They said to Yala, so he said: Do you not see that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says: A Fire whose canopy will encompass them. He said: No, by Him in whose Hand is the soul of Yala, I will never enter it until I am presented before Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and not a drop of it will touch me until I meet Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"18125","Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Amr, meaning Ibn Dinar, from Ata, from Safwan, from his father who said: I heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on the pulpit reciting: And they will cry: O Malik."
"18126","Harun narrated to us, he said: Ibn Wahb informed us, he said: Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Ibn Shihab, from Amr ibn Abdur-Rahman ibn Umayyah, nephew of Yala ibn Umayyah, who narrated to him that his father informed him that Yala ibn Umayyah said: I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with my father on the day of the Conquest, and said to him: O Messenger of Allah, pledge my father for emigration. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Rather I will pledge him for jihad, for emigration has ended."
"18127","Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani narrated to us, Fulayh narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Amr ibn Abdur-Rahman ibn Yala ibn Umayyah, with a chain like it."
"18128","Hushaym narrated to us, Mansur and Abdul-Malik narrated to us, from Ata, from Yala ibn Umayyah who said: A Bedouin came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, wearing a jubbah with a stain of saffron on it, and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have entered ihram in what you see, and the people mock me. And he bowed his head for a while. He said: Then he called him and said: Take off this jubbah from you, and wash off this saffron from you, and do in your umrah as you do in your pilgrimage. Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr, from Ata, from Safwan ibn Yala, from his father who said: A man asked the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was saturated with khaluq perfume and wearing cut garments, and said: I have begun umrah. He said: Take off these, and bathe, and do in your umrah what you do in your pilgrimage."
"18129","Ismail narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj who said: Ata informed me, from Safwan ibn Yala, from Yala ibn Umayyah who said: I fought with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in the army of hardship, and it was among my most trusted deeds in my view. I had a hired worker who fought a man, and one of them bit his companion, so he pulled his finger out, knocking out his front tooth. And he said: Does he leave his hand in your mouth for you to chomp it? He said: I think, as the stallion chomps."
"18130","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Abdul-Malik narrated to us, from Ata, from Yala ibn Umayyah, that he was with Umar on a journey, and he asked Umar to show him the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when revelation was sent down to him. He said: While the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was on a journey with a screen shading him from the sun, a man came to him wearing a jubbah with a stain of saffron on it, and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have entered ihram for umrah, and the people mock me, so how should I do? He said: So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, fell silent and did not answer him. While he was thus, Umar gestured to me with his hand, so I put my head in with them under the screen, and behold the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with red cheeks, with a snorting sound for a while, then it was relieved from him. So he sat up and said: Where is the questioner about umrah? The man stood up to him, so he said: Take off this jubbah of yours from you, and whatever you would do in your pilgrimage when in ihram, do it in your umrah."
"18131","Waki narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Ata, from Yala ibn Umayyah who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, loves modesty and concealment."
"18132","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ibn Yala, from his father, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he arrived, circumambulated the House while wrapping a Hadrami cloak of his under his right arm."
"18133","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Abdul-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman, from Ata, from Safwan ibn Yala ibn Umayyah, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is Modest, Concealing; so if one of you wants to bathe, let him screen himself with something."
